---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { correctionMailto, href, site } from '../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Feature a storage listing | RV Storage Prices';
const description =
  'A featured card is $29 a month, shown first on its city page with a Featured label and a paid-placement note. Cancel anytime. Stripe handles payment.';
const path = '/advertise/';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'Get featured', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: '2026-11-19' }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
const stripeUrl = 'https://buy.stripe.com/cNi28s7X60TU5FgegBfw40c';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Get a featured listing</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Featured placement is $29 a month. It is a paid label on a card that is already in this directory.
      It is not a review, a ranking, or a claim about how full the lot is.
    </p>
    <h2>What $29 a month includes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The card is pinned to the top of its city page.</li>
      <li>The card shows a Featured label.</li>
      <li>The same card says “Paid placement,” so a reader can tell it is an ad.</li>
      <li>Cancel anytime. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.corrections_email}?subject=Cancel%20featured%20listing`}>{site.corrections_email}</a> and the label comes off.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No facility is featured yet. After Stripe confirms the payment, the listing is marked
      <code>featured: true</code> in the city file. Until that edit is published, the card stays in its
      ordinary place with no Featured label.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="action-primary" href={stripeUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Subscribe</a>
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      Payment is handled by Stripe. This page does not store a card number.
      <a href={href('/disclosure/')}>Affiliate disclosure</a> covers other commercial links.
      A correction to the facility facts still goes through <a href={correctionMailto()}>the usual correction email</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
